  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EnDev: Energy Access SME Finance Facilitator (GGF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Energy Access Small- and Medium-sized Enterprises (SME) Finance Facilitator aims to mobilise finance by working with financiers to develop a portfolio of viable loans for SMEs in partner countries that operate in the energy access sector.With little finance available for locally owned companies needing capital between EUR 50,000 and EUR 250,000, the Energy Access SME Finance Facilitator aims to increase the availability of capital in difficult markets. Additionally, it seeks to increase cross-sectoral learning at a portfolio level and possible scaling of best-case practices and insights.The project objective is to unlock inventory financing for at least ten new enterprises in EnDev partner countries, within a 12-month period.</narrative>
  </description>
